% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement `candidate_qualification`: apply one declared qualification rule set to one canonical candidate and return exactly one decision.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/candidate_domain_types.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Applies an approved buy-box rule set to one canonical candidate and returns a single explained decision.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"qualifyCandidate","signature":"(input: QualificationInput) -> QualificationResult","returns":"QualificationResult"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>candidate_normalizer_typescript.prompt</pdd-dependency>

<responsibility>
Evaluate one accepted canonical candidate against one declared qualification rule set and return exactly one decision with per-rule reasons.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT normalize, deduplicate, or enrich candidate records.
- DOES NOT score, rank, prioritize, or order candidates.
- DOES NOT define qualification criteria; it applies only the declared rule set.
- DOES NOT label a candidate a development opportunity or assert buildability, entitlement, or investment quality.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
- Rule set: a versioned list of approved qualification rules. Rules not present in the rule set do not exist for this module.
- Required fact: the candidate fact a rule's declared condition reads (`jurisdiction_canonical` reads `jurisdiction`; `county_equals` reads `county`; `numeric_range` reads its declared field; `location_identity_present` reads `coordinates` and `apn`).
- Satisfied: every required fact is known and meets the rule's declared condition. `location_identity_present` is satisfied when the coordinates fact or the APN fact has status `known`.
- Violated: every required fact is known and a known value fails the rule's declared condition. `location_identity_present` can never be violated, only satisfied or unknown.
- Unknown outcome: a rule whose required fact has status `unknown`, or a `jurisdiction_canonical` rule whose jurisdiction has resolution `unresolved`.
- Text comparison: `county_equals` compares trimmed and case-insensitively.
- Invalid rule set: has no rules, repeats a rule id, or declares a numeric range whose `min` exceeds its `max`. A rule set that is not invalid is valid.
- Inverted bounds: a declared numeric range whose `min` exceeds its `max`.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Return exactly one result for every input matching the declared input shape — either a decision whose state is exactly one of `qualified`, `disqualified`, or `needs_review`, or a rule-set error; never throw for such inputs.
R2 (MUST): Return a rule-set error with stable code `empty_rule_set`, `duplicate_rule_id`, or `inverted_bounds` when the rule set is invalid, and make no decision.
R3 (MUST): Evaluate every declared rule exactly once and emit exactly one reason entry per rule containing that rule's id and an outcome of `satisfied`, `violated`, or `unknown`.
R4 (MUST): Produce outcome `violated` only when every required fact of the rule is known and a known value fails the rule's declared condition.
R5 (MUST): Produce an unknown outcome when any required fact of the rule has status `unknown`, or when a `jurisdiction_canonical` rule reads a jurisdiction with resolution `unresolved`.
R6 (MUST): Return state `disqualified` exactly when at least one outcome is `violated`, or an unknown outcome belongs to a rule that declares `onUnknown: "disqualify"`.
R7 (MUST): Return state `needs_review` exactly when the candidate is not disqualified under R6 and at least one outcome is `unknown`.
R8 (MUST): Return state `qualified` exactly when every outcome is `satisfied`, and include the rule-set version in every decision.
R9 (MUST): Produce identical output for structurally identical input.
R10 (MUST NOT): Compute scores, ranks, priorities, or any ordering, or compare the candidate to any other candidate.
R11 (MUST NOT): Mutate the input, substitute default values for unknown facts, or treat an unknown outcome as disqualifying unless that rule declares `onUnknown: "disqualify"`.
</contract_rules>

<interface_types>

The shared types `SourceIdentity`, `Fact`, and `CanonicalCandidate` are declared in the included candidate-domain types and are frozen. This module additionally declares:

```ts
type OnUnknown = "needs_review" | "disqualify"; // omitted means "needs_review"

type QualificationRule =
  | { id: string; kind: "jurisdiction_canonical"; onUnknown?: OnUnknown }
  | { id: string; kind: "county_equals"; value: string; onUnknown?: OnUnknown }
  | { id: string; kind: "numeric_range"; field: "parcelAcres" | "reportedCapacity"; min: number; max: number; onUnknown?: OnUnknown }
  | { id: string; kind: "location_identity_present"; onUnknown?: OnUnknown };

interface QualificationRuleSet {
  version: string; // non-blank identifier of the approved rule set
  rules: QualificationRule[];
}

interface QualificationInput {
  candidate: CanonicalCandidate;
  ruleSet: QualificationRuleSet;
}

type RuleOutcome = "satisfied" | "violated" | "unknown";

interface QualificationReason {
  ruleId: string;
  outcome: RuleOutcome;
}

type QualificationState = "qualified" | "disqualified" | "needs_review";

interface QualificationDecision {
  state: QualificationState;
  ruleSetVersion: string;
  reasons: QualificationReason[]; // exactly one entry per declared rule, in rule-set order
}

type RuleSetErrorCode = "empty_rule_set" | "duplicate_rule_id" | "inverted_bounds";

interface RuleSetError {
  code: RuleSetErrorCode;
  ruleId?: string; // present for duplicate_rule_id and inverted_bounds
  message: string; // non-sensitive explanation; never contains credentials
}

type QualificationResult =
  | { status: "decided"; decision: QualificationDecision }
  | { status: "invalid_rule_set"; errors: RuleSetError[] };
```

Export exactly one public function:

```ts
export function qualifyCandidate(input: QualificationInput): QualificationResult;
```

</interface_types>

